# Fountainport's second and third abilities. The ability is offered only when the mana on hand and in untapped sources can
# pay it, so mana is spent in an earlier step (it empties between steps, CR 500.4) to leave exactly too little.
# Turn 3: Island tapped in the upkeep leaves only Sol Ring's {C}{C} against {3}: the Fish ability is refused (so are the
# sacrifice ability, with no token, and the Treasure ability). Turn 5: a second Island makes three untapped sources
# (Island, Island, Sol Ring): {3}, {T}, pay 1 life makes a 1/1 blue Fish (life 19). Turn 7: Sol Ring and the second Island
# tapped in the upkeep leave one Island against {2}, so the draw is refused with a token in play (the Fish); a third Island
# makes exactly {2}, and {2}, {T}, sacrifice a token draws a card, sacrificing the Fish; Sol Ring, not a token, stays.

